WEBVTT

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.340
This can't be happening...

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.780
Pascal!

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:32.730
<i>In the city without love</i> <i>only your smile remains.</i>

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:42.730
<i>Hold me tight to crush the loneliness,</i> <i>it's all that stops these pains.</i>

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:53.120
<i>You're constrained by that limit.</i>
<i>Free yourself and break apart the chains.</i>

00:00:53.120 --> 00:01:03.110
<i>It's all gonna burn on down.</i>
<i>Dance to the flames that consume the night.</i>

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:13.290
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright.</i>

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.810
<i>Dance to the end of the night.</i>

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:33.810
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright. Dance!</i>

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:44.490
<i>In the city without love</i>

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:02.890
Pascal!

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.650
Did you see where he fell?

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.520
Yes, roughly.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:07.620
Good.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.060
Ralph and Joseph can search for Pascal.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.650
We'll deal with him.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:19.340
Demetrio. Use this.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:20.400
What is it?

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.670
A powerful bomb handmade by Pascal himself.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:26.640
When you push that button, it'll explode.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.750
It has quite an impact, so it may come in handy.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.910
Thanks. This could help.

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:33.750
Then, I'll get going.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.420
We'll find him for sure.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.350
Good. We're counting on you.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.890
It's time we put an end to this.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:46.530
No...

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:49.000
I'll be the one who takes him down.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.070
"23: Showdown"

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.580
Don't worry.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.780
Pascal wouldn't die that easily.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.210
Right?

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.240
Yeah...

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.220
Will everyone be all right?

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.300
You mustn't cry.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.900
Eljuia!

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:24.060
For now, let us pray for everyone's safety.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:26.360
Okay!

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.210
I never thought my own dad would be the last boss.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.910
Last boss?

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:38.950
The king of evil or something along those lines.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:44.150
Forget your father. Avenging mine doesn't even matter anymore.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:47.560
What matters is stopping that device draining Warp Particles.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.960
You're right.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.480
That's all we need to worry about.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.500
That must be it.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:58.490
Yeah.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.830
Pascal!

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.440
Pascal!

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:12.620
Joseph!

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:13.780
Are you okay?

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:15.480
Why don't we slow down?

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.920
I'll be fine.

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:24.790
There's still thousands of things
I have yet to learn from Pascal!

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.360
To me...

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:31.100
...no, to Endora, that man is invaluable beyond measure!

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:34.370
We have to find him fast.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.940
He's definitely still alive.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:41.040
There's no way he'd go down that easily!

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.940
He can't be dead...

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.490
I know.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.850
I know, Joseph.

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:53.190
Come on. Let's go!

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:54.620
Right!

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.370
Aaron!

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:15.810
There's no end to this.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:19.880
Ibelda... What a monster you've become...

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.320
Yeah.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.080
Mischa!

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:30.220
You little...

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.760
You'll pay for this.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:37.430
Wait.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:41.700
If we attack him from the front, it'll hurt us more than him.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:42.710
But...

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:45.070
What should we do, Demetrio?

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.700
Fortunately, I have a plan.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.850
Felix!

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.250
Thank goodness!

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.280
I...

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.850
Where's Mischa?

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:02.790
Mischa is still off fighting with Demetrio.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.460
I see...

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:06.050
I need to go help.

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:09.370
What are you saying?

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:11.230
You can't go, injured like that.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:14.970
But... I want to fight right beside Demetrio.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:17.600
That's the one purpose left in my life.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:24.050
If I hadn't met Demetrio, it would already be over now.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:27.740
There's no point in living if I can't be of use to him now.

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:31.150
Felix! You have to lie down and rest!

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:34.750
W-Wait a second! The doctor didn't say you could go yet!

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:37.590
I don't care!

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:40.720
Why don't you give it up, Felix?

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:45.630
With injuries like that, you'll only slow them down.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:46.970
Louise...

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.910
Mischa told me what happened.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:54.400
Both you and Louise risked your own lives to protect her.

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:58.810
Sheesh. You and I just don't know when to quit.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.580
Louise... You too?

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:05.790
It might do everyone a favor if we stopped throwing our lives away.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:07.260
Both of us.

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.030
You're right.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:14.960
I'm sorry.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:16.360
It's okay.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:19.440
Thank you...

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.840
Louise.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:28.610
Well, now that's settled, you should drink the secret medicine passed down

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:31.310
in my family for generations.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:34.520
Huh? Was that the thing you just cooked?

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:35.350
Indeed.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.450
That had quite the smell. You drink that?

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:41.320
Of course. I had some of it earlier.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:44.130
That's why I've recovered so well!

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:46.400
Oh... Really?

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.160
I don't need it. Let Louise have it.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.800
You're drinking it too, Felix.

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:55.070
As thanks for saving me, you can have my share.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.370
I never asked for your thanks.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.810
Besides, I never even saved you.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:00.640
You saved me.

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:02.630
--I did not, so drink it.
--You drink it.

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:11.320
It sure looks huge, now that we're close.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:12.580
We need to fly up.

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:27.500
They said it was ruins, but I've never seen any this strange.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:30.510
When I was little, I read a fairy tale about it.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:34.540
In these ruins lives an omnipotent god.

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:36.110
Or so the tale goes.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:38.450
Yeah? A fairy tale?

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:41.250
To think Tir Na Nog actually exists...

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:24.790
So this is...

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:26.820
...Tir Na Nog.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:34.600
It's incredible!

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:36.740
This is straight out of sci-fi.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:38.810
Sci-fi?

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:42.300
Science fiction...
As if you knew what that meant.

00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:45.410
Explain it to me!

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:48.320
I wouldn't even know where to start.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:49.790
Are you mocking me?!

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:52.450
Shut up. You're always saying the same crap.

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:53.650
What was that?!

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:08.100
I guess we smash this thing up.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:09.300
Yeah.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:14.710
Let's do this!

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:16.980
Right!

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:18.540
One, two!

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:22.320
It's damn hard!

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:23.510
Dammit!

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:32.860
How is it so tough?

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:36.160
Hey! Quit slacking off!

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:39.570
This is why newbies are such a pain in the butt, Emilio.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:40.700
What?

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.400
It's gem cleavage.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.070
What's that mean?

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:49.310
Every crystal has a special method which makes it easier to break.

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:50.980
And what's that?

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:54.920
For this one, probably if we jab it from straight above...

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:58.020
Got it!

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:00.160
Be thankful I'm so smart.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.090
Not bad, considering it was you.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.320
Hmph!

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:07.700
Good.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:09.430
Hey, Emilio.

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:13.270
If we can destroy this device, that'll make us heroes.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.500
Heroes?

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.870
We'll be legends forever.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:21.280
I... still don't deserve to be called that.

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:24.250
You're so uptight, Prince.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.880
Isn't it about time you decided already?

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:28.220
Decided what?

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:31.080
If you'll become the king of Endora.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:38.260
Endora's in such a mess now, only a king can fix it.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:39.260
And the only way--

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:41.030
I know that.

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:44.270
I just don't know if I'll be able to do it.

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:48.800
Right now, stopping this device is the one thing I can do.

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:50.030
You're right.

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:16.060
Dad...

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:18.120
Shun, enough of this.

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:35.150
You should know...

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:39.320
Inside of me is a parinblue, just like the one in you.

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:43.760
I will not let you destroy that.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:50.270
That crystal is a special device
I constructed inside of Tir Na Nog.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:55.600
No matter how special it is to you, it's sinister to the world of Endora.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:59.210
Parinblue. Tir Na Nog...

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:05.850
Whether by people of the surface, or the people of Endora, no one understood how to use them.

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:09.850
The only one able to breathe life into them, was me alone.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:13.150
In other words, no one can do what I did.

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:16.360
I told you before.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:22.700
To the surface world, Warp Particles are a valuable resource that we cannot simply give up.

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:24.470
Yeah, you did.

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:27.740
I understand where you're coming from.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.000
But...

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.970
...I still don't agree with it.

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:34.070
Is that what you've always believed?

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:38.180
Or what you believe knowing you came from Endora?

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:42.580
It's only natural that you feel that way now.

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:44.320
Listen to me, Shun.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:49.890
Your mother and I, we raised you believing that you were truly our son.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.860
That will never change.

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:55.030
I... feel the same way.

00:13:55.030 --> 00:13:58.000
Then your decision should be clear.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:02.870
Shun... You should come back and be at my side.

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:04.270
The decision is clear.

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:05.240
Hmm?

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:06.780
I told you before.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:11.210
I will not let Endora become some sacrifice.

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:13.220
Dad...

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:16.410
You met Emilio's father and Delzaine, didn't you?

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:22.060
Using your parinblue, you came here a lot.

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:24.390
You met all sorts of people!

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:28.730
And yet, you think it's okay to sacrifice this world?

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:32.130
How are you able to even consider that?!

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:35.140
I can't understand what you're thinking!

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:38.570
Shun. Let me ask you once more.

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:42.910
Do you have any intention of siding with me... or don't you?

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:57.090
Shun...

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:15.940
We need to distract him and draw his attention.

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:18.910
Then we'll use this guy to blow his head up.

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:22.620
Guidoro?

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:24.020
I'll do it.

00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:27.090
All right.

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:29.620
It's up to you, so make it count.

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:30.630
Right.

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:32.860
Failure is not an option.

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:35.090
Let's go!

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.650
Good! Now go!

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.170
Say your prayers, Ibelda!

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:13.570
It's over for you!

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:27.980
It's over, huh?

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:31.250
It's over for Endora as well.

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:34.190
This entire world is ruined.

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:37.890
So what is it you're even fighting to protect?

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:41.530
Endora... may still have a chance to survive.

00:16:41.530 --> 00:16:47.500
Guidoro... It's as if you actually have some hope for the future.

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:50.410
Hope? Maybe I do...

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:53.240
I haven't entirely abandoned it yet.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.440
What are you saying, Guidoro?

00:16:58.380 --> 00:17:00.850
You asked me once...

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:03.550
Do the Truculent even have any allies?

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:05.950
And?

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:08.720
To answer you, I would say no.

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:10.890
See what I mean?

00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:13.090
However, for me now...

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:16.360
I have comrades fighting with me to protect Endora!

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:34.310
Guidoro!

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:49.590
You fool...

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:53.670
Was that... what I think?

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:54.770
Yeah.

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:56.770
Demetrio must have got him.

00:17:56.770 --> 00:18:01.010
Yes! Pascal's bomb must have saved the day!

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:04.080
Thank goodness. Truly, thank goodness.

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:07.480
I've got to tell Pascal the news right away!

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:11.420
Joseph! This is...

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:12.940
It's Pascal's...

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:16.830
Then, around here...

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:18.260
Pascal!

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:21.820
Pascal!

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:29.940
I see.

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:31.110
Thanks.

00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:32.170
What'd it say?

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:34.010
Was it about Demetrio?

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.810
It seems they defeated Ibelda.

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:36.950
Hurray!

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:38.280
Thank goodness.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:40.880
Is everyone safe then?

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:42.350
Guidoro was...

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:50.230
I'm sorry, Dad.

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:52.990
I... I can't follow in your footsteps.

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:56.400
I see.

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:58.200
That's unfortunate, Shun.

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:07.410
Impossible...

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:10.350
Is that... a Warp Relic?

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:12.850
That's right. It's my Warp Relic.

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:15.820
But you're a human... How could you?!

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:18.320
But I have.

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:23.730
Emilio. Your father Alzerm--he didn't die entirely in vain.

00:19:23.730 --> 00:19:24.690
What?!

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:27.720
I may have borrowed some of his body.

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:31.100
You bastard!

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:34.040
It's bad enough that you killed him! And now this?!

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:36.330
Dad! Are you saying--

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:45.780
Falarion!

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:47.210
You'll pay for this!

00:19:57.530 --> 00:19:59.060
Stop it, Dad!

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:00.620
It's too late.

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:25.820
Emilio!

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:40.000
Shun!

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:41.440
Emilio!

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:47.280
I... I've gotta bring down my dad!

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:48.830
I need your help!

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:04.630
"To be continued..."

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:13.500
<i>I've walked very far, so far</i>

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:23.000
<i>And I'll walk even farther from here</i>

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:45.800
<i>I don't wish for everything to stay the same</i>

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:55.800
<i>Because change is what got me to where I am</i>

00:21:56.410 --> 00:22:04.990
<i>We've walked very far, so far</i>

00:22:04.990 --> 00:22:13.560
<i>We'll go farther than anyone's gone before</i>

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:22.100
<i>Each of us can change the world</i>

00:22:22.100 --> 00:22:31.270
<i>That's why I smile at you</i>
